{"sqft":"","meters":[{"id":"b7cd5123-b2e0-42ea-be62-c1c522240c94","rate":"","esiId":"","address":"3215 West Loop 820 South, Fort Worth, TX 76116, United States","endDate":""}],"country":"United States","ownerId":"l.patterson@nodalpoint.io","enriched":false,"occupancy":"","postal_code":"76116","import_batch":"2026-04-27T18:22:37.575Z","headcount_max":50,"headcount_min":10,"headcount_raw":"10-50","import_source":"bulk_import_contact","annual_revenue":"17000000","apollo_raw_data":{"id":"5e57c5f7d2bd68000120dc7a","zip":"76116","city":"Fort Worth","name":"Av-DEC® - Aviation Devices & Electronic Components, LLC","state":"Texas","domain":"avdec.com","address":"3215 West Loop 820 South, Fort Worth, Texas 76116, US","country":"United States","logoUrl":"https://zenprospect-production.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/pictures/67c4466a5c5f1f00013a0f56/picture","revenue":"","website":"http://www.avdec.com","industry":"airlines/aviation","linkedin":"http://www.linkedin.com/company/avdec","location":"Fort Worth, Texas, United States","employees":"10-50","companyType":"airlines/aviation","description":"Av-DEC® - Aviation Devices & Electronic Components, LLC is a technical design and manufacturing company based in Fort Worth, Texas. Founded in 1997, Av-DEC specializes in corrosion prevention solutions tailored for the aerospace industry. The company focuses on developing high-performance, non-hazardous polyurethane-based sealants and gaskets that address corrosion challenges throughout aviation production, installation, repair, and maintenance.

Av-DEC's product offerings include antenna and specialty gaskets, injectable sealants, polyurethane rolled sealants (PRS®), and sprayable sealants. These products are designed to provide effective moisture barriers and long-term corrosion protection for various aircraft components. The company serves a wide range of customers, including major OEMs, airlines, business jets, and military branches, and has received several industry awards for its performance and innovation. Av-DEC is committed to exceeding customer expectations and leading the industry in responsiveness to their needs.","foundedYear":1997,"companyPhone":"+1 817-738-9161"},"headcount_label":"10-50","headcount_source":"apollo_enrichment","apollo_enriched_at":"2026-06-09T18:22:10.267Z","intelligenceProfile":{"version":1,"evidence":["Av-DEC® - Aviation Devices & Electronic Components, LLC is a technical design and manufacturing company based in Fort Worth, Texas. Founded in 1997, Av-DEC specializes in corrosion prevention solutions tailored for the…","GO!. PRODUCTS SUPPORT TRAINING INNOVATION ABOUT US Home Error 404 Page not found Oops! Page Not Found Sorry, the page you requested (/press) could not be found on our site. It may have been moved, deleted, or possible t…"],"confidence":"medium","companyType":"industrial manufacturer","generatedAt":"2026-06-09T18:23:06.811Z","sourceKinds":["web"],"facilityType":"plant / production facility","powerKeywords":["production lines","process equipment","HVAC"],"operatingModel":"production facility","industryCluster":"manufacturing","identityKeywords":["manufacturing","production","industrial"],"talkTrackGuardrails":["No retail language","No office-only language"]},"source_company_fields":{"sic_code":"3669","naics_code":"481","company_city":"Fort Worth","company_state":"Texas","company_country":"United States","company_phone_1":"817.738.9161","company_industry":"Aviation & Aerospace","company_location":"3215 West Loop 820 South, Fort Worth, TX 76116, United States","company_post_code":"76116","company_state_abbr":"TX","company_description":"Av-DEC - The World Leader in the Science of Corrosion Prevention.
Preventing aircraft corrosion is what Av-DEC does. The prevention of corrosion can be done using non-hazardous, durable, and easily applied products. This is the reason the company's engineers have continuously sought out better solutions to ensure corrosion is comprehensively eliminated and the aircraft is protected for the long haul. The Av-DEC story is one of constant improvement to help the aviation industry enhance aircraft safety through corrosion prevention.","company_staff_count":"125","company_founded_date":"1997","company_name_cleaned":"Av-DEC","company_revenue_range":"$5M - $20M","company_annual_revenue":"17000000","company_li_profile_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/avdec","company_website_domain":"avdec.com","company_country_alpha_2":"US","company_country_alpha_3":"USA","company_country_numeric":"840","company_staff_count_range":"51 - 200 employees"},"intelligenceBriefAngles":{"all":{"loadFactor":{"headline":"Managing Load and Peak Charges for Av-DEC's Production Facility","talk_track":"Having those specialized manufacturing processes running can create a spiky load profile, especially during startup sequences, which can lead to higher charges on the bill. I'm curious, how do y'all monitor and manage the load factor of your Fort Worth facility, or is that pretty much on autopilot?"},"esgRenewables":{"headline":"Integrating Renewables for Av-DEC's Sustainability Goals","talk_track":"Many manufacturing companies are looking to hit sustainability goals by integrating renewables without paying a green premium, especially with their production footprint. I'm curious, how do y'all approach incorporating renewable energy into your operations, or is that side of things pretty much on autopilot?"},"renewalTiming":{"headline":"Optimizing Av-DEC's Electricity Contract Renewal Window","talk_track":"Most manufacturing companies find that their electricity contracts auto-renew without much review, potentially missing out on better terms for their production needs. I'm curious, how do y'all approach the renewal window for your electricity agreements, or is that side of things pretty much handled?"},"demandResponse":{"headline":"Av-DEC's Opportunity for Demand Response in ERCOT","talk_track":"With the kind of production work Av-DEC does, there might be opportunities to get paid for being flexible during ERCOT grid stress events, especially during the summer. I'm curious, how do y'all evaluate participating in demand response programs, or is that side of things pretty much on autopilot?"},"budgetCertainty":{"headline":"Budget Stability and Price-Spike Protection for Av-DEC's Manufacturing Operations","talk_track":"When y'all are running the manufacturing lines for your aerospace sealants and gaskets, those production ramps can sometimes create unexpected spikes that impact the budget. I'm curious, how do y'all ensure budget certainty over the next 24-36 months, or is that pretty much on autopilot?"},"billingOptimization":{"headline":"Auditing Av-DEC's Electricity Bills for Accuracy and Optimization","talk_track":"Often times, the detailed line items on manufacturing electricity bills, especially demand fees from production ramps, can have errors or hidden charges that go unnoticed. I'm curious, how closely do y'all audit your electricity bills for accuracy and potential overcharges, or is that pretty much handled?"}},"primary":"demandResponse","secondary":"loadFactor"},"intelligenceAudienceProfile":null,"intelligenceBriefingContext":{"confidence":"medium","personaLens":"No specific contact selected; use owner/controller/facilities-friendly language.","problemFrame":"Often times for a manufacturing operation, startup sequences, production ramps, shift-driven peaks, and peak charges on the bill can all hit the meter during the same busy window.","signalReason":"Company context from website, CRM account facts, and industry pattern","questionFrame":"I'm curious, how do y'all tell whether startup sequences, production ramps, and shift-driven peaks are what moved the bill that month, or is that side of things pretty much handled?","companyIdentity":"Manufacturing operation","structuredFacts":{"equipment":[],"activities":["Production work"],"avoidAngles":[],"sourceTerms":["Production work","Startup sequences","Production ramps","Shift-driven peaks","Peak charges on the bill","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Transmission liability","Budget visibility"],"businessModel":"Manufacturing operation","energyDrivers":["Startup sequences","Production ramps","Shift-driven peaks","Peak charges on the bill","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Transmission liability","Budget visibility"],"customerContext":[]},"forbiddenLanguage":["Do not use jargon like demand ratchet, billing floor, load factor, base load, or throughput.","Do not mention scraping, LinkedIn, Google, RSS, or internal CRM notes.","Do not sound like a commodity broker or say you can save money."],"operationalDrivers":["Startup sequences","Production ramps","Shift-driven peaks","Peak charges on the bill","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Transmission liability","Budget visibility"]},"intelligenceHierarchyContext":null}

{"sqft":"","mills":"","meters":[{"id":"bc2fa2b3-b6e3-4917-9678-7e1cd2c1ba37","rate":"","esiId":"","address":"3200 Olympus Blvd Suite 100, Dallas, TX 75201, United States","endDate":""},{"id":"a2dbb272-d9f8-4108-ac03-cc07a5601c93","rate":"","esiId":"","address":"3200 Olympus Blvd, Suite 200, Dallas, Texas 75019, US","endDate":""}],"country":"United States","ownerId":"l.patterson@nodalpoint.io","enriched":false,"occupancy":"","postal_code":"75201","import_batch":"2026-04-27T18:24:20.036Z","headcount_max":1000,"headcount_min":500,"headcount_raw":"500-1,000","import_source":"bulk_import_contact","annual_revenue":"300000000","apollo_raw_data":{"id":"54a139ac69702dc8e47a5a00","zip":"75019","city":"Dallas","name":"BNSF Logistics","state":"Texas","domain":"bnsflogistics.com","address":"3200 Olympus Blvd, Suite 200, Dallas, Texas 75019, US","country":"United States","logoUrl":"https://zenprospect-production.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/pictures/69ac22c4d2009d000174c1c4/picture","revenue":"1B","website":"http://www.bnsflogistics.com","industry":"logistics & supply chain","linkedin":"http://www.linkedin.com/company/bnsflogistics","location":"Dallas, Texas, United States","employees":"500-1000","companyType":"logistics & supply chain","description":"BNSF Logistics is a third-party logistics provider and a subsidiary of Burlington Northern Santa Fe, LLC, part of Berkshire Hathaway. Founded in 2002 and based in Dallas, Texas, the company specializes in multi-modal transportation solutions, including truck, rail, and barge services. With a workforce of approximately 661-696 employees across 15 U.S. offices, BNSF Logistics has experienced significant growth through both organic expansion and strategic acquisitions.

The company offers a range of services, including end-to-end supply chain management, freight brokerage, and custom engineering for complex cargo needs. Key offerings include cross-docking, transloading, and expedited truck and rail services. BNSF Logistics is known for its strong rail-truck integration and targets industries that require high-volume, just-in-time delivery. Its client roster includes notable companies such as Frito Lay, Wal-Mart de Mexico, U.S. Borax, and The Home Depot, showcasing its expertise in large-scale logistics and cross-border operations.","foundedYear":2002,"companyPhone":"+1 800-275-8521"},"headcount_label":"500-1,000","headcount_source":"account_update","apollo_enriched_at":"2026-06-09T18:40:48.616Z","intelligenceProfile":{"version":1,"evidence":["BNSF Logistics is a third-party logistics provider and a subsidiary of Burlington Northern Santa Fe, LLC, part of Berkshire Hathaway. Founded in 2002 and based in Dallas, Texas, the company specializes in multi-modal tr…","BNSF Logistics ©2025 HQ: 3501 Olympus Blvd. BNSF Logistics ©2025 HQ: 3501 Olympus Blvd. – Suite 350 Dallas, TX 75019 Phone: 1 (800) 275-8521 Resources Transport Terms & Conditions Downloads & Case Studies Privacy Statem…","Bnsf Logistics website Facility and Billing Intel. Resources Contact & Support Careers HOME TRANSPORTATION ABOUT REQUEST A QUOTE Transporting Bigger, Longer, Heavier, Complicated Cargo? We design custom solutions to sim…"],"confidence":"medium","companyType":"freight forwarder and logistics operator","generatedAt":"2026-06-09T18:42:49.519Z","sourceKinds":["web"],"facilityType":"logistics office / yard","powerKeywords":["dock activity","material handling","HVAC"],"operatingModel":"multi-site logistics network","industryCluster":"logistics","identityKeywords":["logistics","cargo","supply chain","distribution","freight forwarding"],"talkTrackGuardrails":["No manufacturing language","No plant language"]},"source_company_fields":{"sic_code":"4731","naics_code":"336","company_city":"Dallas","company_state":"Texas","company_country":"United States","company_phone_1":"800.275.8521","company_industry":"Logistics & Supply Chain","company_location":"3200 Olympus Blvd Suite 100, Dallas, TX 75201, United States","company_post_code":"75201","company_state_abbr":"TX","company_description":"BNSF Logistics, a Berkshire Hathaway Company, is the premier logistics and warehouse provider solving the most complex cargo challenges the US Shipping community faces and will face in the 21st century. Through innovative design, engineering, multi-modal execution, asset deployment, unique rail partnerships and all-encompassing customer service, BNSF logistics provides proven timesaving and budget friendly solutions that overcome our customer’s obstacles in ways no other 3PL can.  
At BNSF Logistics, We Deliver What Matters to You.","company_staff_count":"750","company_founded_date":"2002","company_name_cleaned":"Bnsf Logistics","company_revenue_range":"$100M - $500M","company_annual_revenue":"300000000","company_li_profile_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/bnsflogistics","company_website_domain":"bnsflogistics.com","company_country_alpha_2":"US","company_country_alpha_3":"USA","company_country_numeric":"840","company_staff_count_range":"501 - 1,000 employees"},"intelligenceBriefAngles":{"all":{"loadFactor":{"headline":"Managing Load Spikes from BNSF Logistics' Automation and HVAC","talk_track":"The combined impact of automation, dock activity, and HVAC in a large distribution center can create significant load spikes that drive up peak charges. I'm curious, how do y'all manage those shifting usage patterns to avoid higher peak pricing hours, or is that pretty much on autopilot?"},"esgRenewables":{"headline":"Achieving Sustainability Goals for BNSF Logistics Without Green Premiums","talk_track":"Many logistics companies are looking to hit sustainability targets by incorporating renewables without paying a premium on their electricity costs. I'm curious, how do y'all explore options for integrating renewable energy into your operations without increasing your budget, or is that side of things pretty much on autopilot?"},"renewalTiming":{"headline":"Optimizing Electricity Contract Renewals for BNSF Logistics","talk_track":"Many logistics companies find that their electricity contracts auto-renew without a thorough market review, potentially missing out on better terms. I'm curious, how do y'all approach auditing your electricity renewal terms, or is that side of things pretty much handled?"},"demandResponse":{"headline":"Demand Response Opportunities for BNSF Logistics in ERCOT","talk_track":"During periods of grid stress in ERCOT, distribution centers with flexible operations can get paid for reducing their electricity use. I'm curious, how do y'all evaluate opportunities to participate in demand response programs, or is that side of things pretty much handled?"},"budgetCertainty":{"headline":"Budget Certainty for BNSF Logistics' Distribution Operations","talk_track":"With the constant movement of goods and equipment in a logistics hub, it's easy for energy costs to fluctuate unexpectedly, making budget forecasting a challenge. I'm curious, how do y'all ensure budget certainty for your electricity spend over the next 24-36 months, or is that pretty much on autopilot?"},"billingOptimization":{"headline":"Auditing BNSF Logistics' Electricity Bills for Accuracy","talk_track":"Complex commercial electricity bills often contain pass-through charges and demand fee calculations that can be difficult to verify for accuracy. I'm curious, how do y'all ensure all the line items on your electricity bills are correct, or is that pretty much handled?"}},"primary":"demandResponse","secondary":"billingOptimization"},"intelligenceAudienceProfile":null,"intelligenceBriefingContext":{"confidence":"medium","personaLens":"No specific contact selected; use owner/controller/facilities-friendly language.","problemFrame":"Often times for a distribution operation, cooling and door activity, dock door timing, automation peaks, and HVAC load can all hit the meter during the same busy window.","signalReason":"Company context from website, CRM account facts, and industry pattern","questionFrame":"I'm curious, how do y'all tell whether cooling and door activity, dock door timing, and automation peaks are what moved the bill that month, or is that side of things pretty much handled?","companyIdentity":"Distribution operation","structuredFacts":{"equipment":[],"activities":[],"avoidAngles":[],"sourceTerms":["Cooling and door activity","Dock door timing","Automation peaks","HVAC load","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Peak charges on the bill","Budget visibility"],"businessModel":"Distribution operation","energyDrivers":["Cooling and door activity","Dock door timing","Automation peaks","HVAC load","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Peak charges on the bill","Budget visibility"],"customerContext":[]},"forbiddenLanguage":["Do not use jargon like demand ratchet, billing floor, load factor, base load, or throughput.","Do not mention scraping, LinkedIn, Google, RSS, or internal CRM notes.","Do not sound like a commodity broker or say you can save money."],"operationalDrivers":["Cooling and door activity","Dock door timing","Automation peaks","HVAC load","Peak charges that stick on the bill","Peak charges on the bill","Budget visibility"]},"intelligenceHierarchyContext":null}

